## Prompt 1 — Logo (Combined Flutter + Plugin Identity)

> **Use with:** Midjourney, DALL-E 3, or Ideogram

```
A minimal, flat-design logo for a Flutter plugin called "Power GeoJSON".

Combine two visual identities:
1. The Flutter hummingbird — represented as a sleek, geometric outline or silhouette in sky blue (#027DFD).
2. GeoJSON / spatial data — represented by a subtle globe wireframe, map pin, or coordinate grid lines, using deep blue (#1E00FD) and translucent blue (#2195F3).

The two elements should merge into a single cohesive logomark — for example, the Flutter bird shape formed FROM map grid lines, or the bird perched on a stylized globe outline, or the bird's wings doubling as polygon/polyline paths on a map.

Style:
- Flat, vector, no gradients — think developer tool icon
- Dark background (#0D1117, GitHub dark) with the icon colored in blue (#027DFD) and a subtle orange (#FF9800) accent for one small detail (e.g. a map pin tip, a data point dot)
- Monoline or duotone only
- Clean negative space, no text in the icon
- Square aspect ratio, suitable as a pub.dev package icon or GitHub repo avatar
- Feels like a modern open-source dev tool logo (similar to Supabase, Vercel, Turbo)

Output: single icon on a transparent or dark (#0D1117) background, 1024×1024px, PNG.
```

### Variant B — Light Background

```
Same as above, but on a clean white (#FFFFFF) background. The icon should use #1E00FD (deep blue) as the primary stroke color, with #027DFD (Flutter blue) as a secondary fill, and a single small orange (#FF9800) accent. Minimal, flat, no shadows.
```

### Variant C — Monochrome / One-Color

```
A single-color monochrome version of the Power GeoJSON logo — a geometric merge of a Flutter bird silhouette and GeoJSON map coordinates or a globe wireframe. 
Single color: white on transparent, or #027DFD on white. 
Ultra-minimal, works at 16×16 favicon size. No text, no gradients.
```

---

## Prompt 2 — Modern Example UI Screenshot

> **Use with:** DALL-E 3, Midjourney, or Ideogram (or v0.dev for code)

```
A high-fidelity UI screenshot of a modern Flutter mobile app that demonstrates a geospatial data plugin. Dark theme (#0D1117 background).

The screen shows:
- A full-bleed interactive map (OpenStreetMap or dark-themed mapbox style tiles) taking up ~65% of the screen
- On the map: translucent blue (#2195F3 at 40% opacity) polygons with deep blue (#1E00FD) borders, orange (#FF9800) polylines tracing routes, and small red (#F44336) circular map markers clustered together
- A floating bottom sheet / card (glassmorphism, frosted glass, rounded corners 16px) with:
  - A small header row: the plugin logo icon + "Power GeoJSON" in a monospace/dev font (JetBrains Mono or Fira Code), white text
  - Below that: a compact list of 2–3 GeoJSON feature items, each with a colored dot indicator (blue for polygon, orange for line, red for point) and a truncated feature name in Inter or SF Pro font, muted gray (#8B949E)
  - A subtle "Load GeoJSON →" button in Flutter blue (#027DFD), pill-shaped

- Top of screen: a minimal app bar (transparent/blur) with a hamburger menu icon and "Example" title in Inter Medium, white
- Status bar: standard dark mode iOS/Android status bar

Typography:
- Headings: Inter Semi-Bold or SF Pro, white (#E6EDF3)
- Body/labels: Inter Regular, muted gray (#8B949E)
- Code/badges: JetBrains Mono or Fira Code, 12px, in a subtle dark chip (#161B22)

Color palette (strictly):
- Background: #0D1117
- Surface/cards: #161B22 with glassmorphism blur
- Primary: #027DFD (Flutter blue)
- Polygon fill: #2195F3 at 40%
- Polygon border: #1E00FD
- Polyline: #FF9800
- Markers: #F44336
- Text primary: #E6EDF3
- Text secondary: #8B949E
- Accent glow: subtle #027DFD glow on the button

Aesthetic: ultra-modern, developer-focused, dark mode, minimal UI chrome, premium feel — like a Raycast or Linear app crossed with a mapping tool. No placeholder text, everything looks real and functional.

Output: iPhone 15 Pro frame, 1290×2796px or similar portrait mobile resolution.
```

### Variant B — Light Theme

```
Same layout as above but light theme:
- Background: #FFFFFF
- Surface/cards: #F6F8FA with subtle shadow (no glassmorphism)
- Text primary: #1F2328
- Text secondary: #656D76
- Map tiles: standard bright OpenStreetMap
- Same polygon/polyline/marker colors
- Button: #027DFD on white, subtle shadow
- Font: Inter for UI, JetBrains Mono for code
- Clean, airy, like the GitHub or Linear light mode
```

